issues.body:
Testing #339645

- Configure a policy with `allowOutbound: true`
- configure user settings that disallow network
```
	"chat.agent.sandbox.network.allowNetwork": false,
```

- ask to access 'www.yahoo.com': works.
- 
Shouldn't the stricter choice be followed?  

```
{
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": true,
    "allowBypass": false,
    "sandboxMcpServers": true,
    "sandboxLspServers": true,
    "allowDevToolAccess": false,
    "userPolicy": {
      "network": {
        "allowOutbound": true,
        "allowLocalNetwork": false
      }
    }
  }
}
}

```

Testing #339645

- have this policy file, note `"enabled": false, allowOutbound: false`
- in the settings have
```
	"chat.agent.sandbox.network.allowedDomains": [
		"www.nzz.ch"
	],
```

- open a chat, enabled sandbox with `/sandbox enable`, make a network request to 'www.nzz.ch', works

Shouldn't this be restricted by the policy file due to `allowOutbound: false`?
```
{
  "sandbox": {
    "enabled": false,
    "allowBypass": false,
    "sandboxMcpServers": true,
    "sandboxLspServers": true,
    "allowDevToolAccess": false,
    "userPolicy": {
      "network": {
        "allowOutbound": false,
        "allowLocalNetwork": false
      }
    }
  }
}
```

